Create the AscendKeep battle screen background — the full-screen backdrop shown behind the Core, the Voidborn and the projectiles during an actual run.

This is not a tileable texture swatch (see arena-background.json for that). This is a single fixed portrait image, framed exactly for the game's play area, sitting behind everything else — it must never distract from or compete with the gameplay sprites on top of it.

Design:

* true top-down orthographic view, matching the camera the Core and Voidborn are drawn in;
* a circular ancient stone arena fills most of the frame, centered, large enough that Voidborn walking in from its edge toward the middle read as standing on solid ground;
* cracked, weathered stone floor, desaturated gray, with subtle circular architectural rings radiating outward from the center like ripples;
* extremely faint cyan runes embedded in the stone, only visible up close, never competing with the Core's own glow at the center;
* the outermost edge of the arena fades into near-black Void — no visible horizon, no walls, no sky;
* the very center, where the Core itself will be placed by the game, must be kept plain and slightly darker so the Core sprite reads clearly on top of it;
* extremely restrained detail overall — this sits *behind* moving gameplay objects, so it must never be busy or high-contrast enough to hurt readability.

Composition:

* portrait orientation, 720×1280 (9:16), no cropping needed for this exact frame;
* the top ~80px strip and bottom ~110px strip of the frame (where the HUD bars sit) should be the darkest, plainest part of the image — near-black, minimal detail — so UI text stays legible over it;
* no tower, no Core, no Voidborn, no projectiles, no characters;
* no UI, no text, no logo, no frame, no watermark;
* no directional lighting, no lens effects, no vignette stronger than the natural darkening toward the Void at the edges.

[INCLUDE ASCENDKEEP VISUAL STYLE BIBLE]
